# ☁ AWS Services Used

| Service | Purpose |
|----------|----------|
| API Gateway | REST API |
| Lambda | Business Logic |
| DynamoDB | NoSQL Database |
| IAM | Security |
| CloudWatch | Logging & Monitoring |
| SNS | Email Notifications |
| Terraform | Infrastructure Provisioning |
| Jenkins | CI/CD |

---

# 🌐 API Endpoints

## Get All Employees

```
GET /employee
```

---

## Get Employee By ID

```
GET /employee/{id}
```

---

## Create Employee

```
POST /employee
```

Example

```json
{
  "EmployeeID":"101",
  "Name":"Suren",
  "Role":"DevOps Engineer"
}
```

---

## Update Employee

```
PUT /employee/{id}
```

---

## Delete Employee

```
DELETE /employee/{id}
```

---

# 🖥 Prerequisites

- AWS Account
- IAM User with Programmatic Access
- AWS CLI
- Terraform
- Python 3
- Jenkins
- Git

---

# ⚙ Deployment Steps

## Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/suren00-77-99/lambda-project.git

cd lambda-project
```

---

## Configure AWS

```bash
aws configure
```

---

## Initialize Terraform

```bash
cd Terraform

terraform init
```

---

## Validate

```bash
terraform validate
```

---

## Plan

```bash
terraform plan
```

---

## Deploy

```bash
terraform apply
```

---

## Destroy Infrastructure

```bash
terraform destroy
```

---

# 🔄 Jenkins CI/CD Workflow

The deployment pipeline performs the following stages:

- Checkout Source Code
- Terraform Init
- Terraform Format
- Terraform Validate
- Terraform Plan
- Manual Approval
- Terraform Apply
- Package Lambda
- Archive Artifacts

A separate Jenkins pipeline is provided to safely destroy the infrastructure after manual approval.

---

# 📊 Monitoring

CloudWatch is configured to collect:

- Lambda execution logs
- API Gateway logs
- Lambda error metrics

SNS is used to send email notifications when CloudWatch alarms are triggered.

---

# 🔐 IAM Security

The Lambda execution role follows the **Principle of Least Privilege** and has permissions only for:

- DynamoDB
- CloudWatch Logs
- SNS Publish

---

# 📸 Sample Response

```
GET /employee
```

```json
[
  {
    "EmployeeID": "101",
    "Name": "Suren",
    "Role": "DevOps Engineer"
  }
]
```

If no records exist in DynamoDB, the API returns:

```json
[]
```

